\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Anytime-valid certificate validation, exactly as recorded in \texttt {experiments/kbound/theory\_validation/val\_thm3\_evalue\_results.json} ($\alpha =0.1$, wealth threshold $1/\alpha =10$, horizon $2000$, $20{,}000$ Monte Carlo runs per cell, seed $0$, bet cap $c=0.5$; power rounded to three decimals, mean stopping times to integers). The worst-case anytime false-adapt rate across all nine null settings is $0.0626\le \alpha =0.1$; the results file's verdict field records \texttt {controlled:\,true}.}}{56}{table.5.1}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Knowability hierarchy of distribution shifts for label-free adapt/freeze decisions, as drawn in the paper. The boundary is evidence-identifiability: some shifts are knowable, some are not, and a valid certificate abstains across the boundary. The label-shift row follows the black-box shift estimation conditions of \cite {lipton2018detecting}.}}{59}{table.5.2}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces The certified map of regimes assembled by Chapters~\ref {ch:theory1} and~\ref {ch:theory2}: each row pairs a regime with its governing result, the exact form of its guarantee, and the machine-checked validator or experiment that exercises it.}}{67}{table.5.3}%
